/P 45 0 R
/E (Thecase study demonstrated the major limitations that can arise when low-code platforms are applied to )
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
223 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 45 0 R
/E (complex enterprise requirements, namely performance and scalability, complex business logic, system integration, customisation, security and governance, AI and advanced technology, vendor or platform dependency, and data management. It also showed how a hybrid low-code/pro-code approach can address requirements beyond standard low-code capabilities.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
224 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 45 0 R
/T (Conclusion)
/E (Conclusion)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
225 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 45 0 R
/E (Low-code platforms offer speed and simplicity for standard business applications, but their limitations become more significant as enterprise complexity increases. For an application such as the Enterprise Gym Membership Management System, standard functionality can be built quickly using low-code, while demanding requirements in logic, integration, security, scale and advanced technology may need pro-code extensions. It is therefore important to understand the limitations of a platform before selecting a development approach, so that the chosen approach matches the requirements of the enterprise application.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
